{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1525405-damage","id":1525405,"title":"Damage!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-13T11:31:20-08:00","id":1525405,"title":"Damage!?","content":"Con someone please give me an example of how to run damage both with Scale and without?<br /> I think I have it, then a few days goes by and I read something else and I get confused. Part of the confusion I think comes from the new vernacular ie; enhancement,etcc.<br /> <br /> Say I have a sawed-off double barrel shotgun and I fire it all in one blast, what's the damage I do? IS the weapon Scaled up? if so how much and what does that now empower it to do? <br /> <br /> I get confused because I read that you can only buy the inflict damage one time, but I see some weapons that add +1 to the enhancement. A knife and a pistol do the same damage? How is damage calculated?<br /> <br /> OMG it is certainly different than V1.<br /> Please help me clarify this in my head, ELI5 because I want to like this version but this part is destroying my mind!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28265-asche","name":"Asche","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28265_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T13:07:38-08:00","id":1525408,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not a complex system, the problem is we came to it with experience with similar systems that use different damage systems.<br /> <br /> Let me start from the beginning, you roll only once per turn, so in your example you pick your gun and roll Aim + Dex.<br /> Let\u2019s just ignore the tags to start, the fun has 1 enhancement, so if you roll that many dice and at least 1 rolls 7 or more (8 if you are not a Nova) you gain 1 extra success (the enhancement).<br /> <br /> If your target has defense 2 and soft armor 1, and you roll 3 successes and got 1 enhancement from the gun, you spend 2 successes to hit the target, but hit doesn\u2019t mean cause injury. To cause injury you need to buy the Cause Injury stunt that cost the soft armor of the target (possibly 0, 1 in this case). You don\u2019t need to buy it, you can just hit it and not hurt it, for example buying other stunts, as described ahead.<br /> <br /> After hitting and buying the cause injury, you have 1 remaining success that you can use to buy other stunts. You can cause the target unbalanced, or bleed or fall, what ever but it will be a complication 1 (from the cost 1 you pay) that may force the target to spend one of its successes to avoid the effects, for example, if not buying it the target gets prone or can\u2019t see you next round, or what ever. You can also give your friends some advantage, for example spending the success to add an enhancement to the next player to attack the target.<br /> <br /> If you had roll 7 successes you could spend 2 to beat the defense, 1 to buy the injury and 4 to buy the critical stunt, causing one additional injury in the target.<br /> <br /> Now on scale, regular weapons (those that are not part of vehicles or that doesn\u2019t have the Heacy Weapon tag) are always scale 1. A character using a scale weapon can buy the cause injury stunt once again for each scale the weapon have over the target. So if you have a tank cannon (scale 4) you can cause 4 injuries to the human target, buying cause injury once and 3 more times for the 3 scales above, and can buy the critical in addition to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T16:48:46-08:00","id":1525412,"title":"","content":"The inflicted condition for a tank cannon on a human body is also known as &quot;chunky salsa&quot;. (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T17:16:06-08:00","id":1525413,"title":"","content":"So I was hoping I was misunderstanding, but in short, unless its a scale weapon, the absolute most damage can be done in one shot/hit/whatever, is 2 damage?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28265-asche","name":"Asche","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28265_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T17:30:30-08:00","id":1525414,"title":"","content":"Positive. Well, Aberrants can do much more with their scale, so it\u2019s not that limited, but yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T17:32:18-08:00","id":1525415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asche</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1525405-damage?p=1525413#post1525413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was hoping I was misunderstanding, but in short, unless its a scale weapon, the absolute most damage can be done in one shot/hit/whatever, is 2 damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, unless Scale comes into play you can only do levels of damage in a single attack.<br /> <br /> Trinity Continuum is a very cinematic system, it's not trying to accurately simulate weapons and things. On the player side of things, since damage heals very slowly even one or two levels can be a big deal. On the Antagonist side of things, the threats are meant to last a few rounds or stand up against a few PCs. Also remember Minor Characters, they're basically mooks and if they are hit at all they're Taken Out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T17:39:53-08:00","id":1525416,"title":"","content":"Hmm.. I see. I'll have to see if it's tweakable. My gang has grown attached to the fact that anyone can get lucky and kill their characters with a lucky shot, we like the grit. One guy loves to get his toons killed and reroll a new one every so often.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28265-asche","name":"Asche","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28265_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T17:43:42-08:00","id":1525417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asche</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1525405-damage?p=1525416#post1525416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.. I see. I'll have to see if it's tweakable. My gang has grown attached to the fact that anyone can get lucky and kill their characters with a lucky shot, we like the grit. One guy loves to get his toons killed and reroll a new one every so often.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your replies.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your players like the current way you could just stick with it. Are there any issues you were seeing that caused you to reread the rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T18:05:46-08:00","id":1525418,"title":"","content":"Eh, we saw version 2 and liked some of the new rules like scale and Tier and we were thinking of changing over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28265-asche","name":"Asche","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28265_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T19:13:44-08:00","id":1525419,"title":"","content":"Perhaps confusingly, Onyx Path is working on a new version of the Storypath rules called Storypath Ultra. There is a booklet on drivethrurpg that has some advice on how to convert other games to the new rules if you want (there aren't plans to do a new edition of any trinity continuum games currently). The combat rules in Ultra are a bit different, notably around damage, armor, and health and might give you ideas on how to make changes.<br /> <br /> In the Storypath Nexus section on drivethrurpg there are fan supplements, there might be some stuff there you could pick up for a few bucks that might help. I think one or two have some tweaks to combat rules, not sure if they would get you the exact feel you want, but they could spark some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}